WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.585 --> 00:00:03.003
Do you know what it feels like?

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:08.217
It's like... I've woken up
in someone else's life.

00:00:12.054 --> 00:00:15.265
Surface is a thriller about identity

00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:18.352
and about uncovering
the truth about yourself.

00:00:18.435 --> 00:00:21.605
Who you were, who you are,
and who you really wanna be.

00:00:22.648 --> 00:00:24.983
Sophie had a traumatic brain injury,

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:28.278
and it's really her putting the pieces
of her life back together.

00:00:28.362 --> 00:00:30.239
So she wakes up in this perfect life,

00:00:30.322 --> 00:00:33.033
but something, at the core,
she knows is wrong.

00:00:33.325 --> 00:00:34.826
If my life was so perfect...

00:00:35.536 --> 00:00:37.079
why did I try to end it?

00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:41.041
So this question is eating at her
from the beginning of the series.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.254
Everything starts to crack
and starts to sort of shake and change.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:48.924
All these characters
are kind of playing two sides.

00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:51.134
There's the version
that the audience knows,

00:00:51.218 --> 00:00:52.553
and then there's the real version.

00:00:52.636 --> 00:00:54.972
For Sophie, this duality of...

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:58.141
Is she actually who everybody
thinks she is?

00:00:58.225 --> 00:01:00.310
And is she a good person?

00:01:00.394 --> 00:01:02.771
And is she capable of bad things?

00:01:02.855 --> 00:01:04.231
...is really interesting.

00:01:04.314 --> 00:01:05.732
Hey, let me take that.

00:01:05.816 --> 00:01:10.362
James is madly in love with Sophie
and would do anything for her.

00:01:10.445 --> 00:01:15.158
But as time goes on, Sophie starts
to question his authenticity.

00:01:16.493 --> 00:01:19.204
Baden's definitely a guy
who's a little bit mysterious.

00:01:19.288 --> 00:01:21.999
Why did you say that about my husband?

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:24.877
It's usually the person who's closest
to the victim that's responsible.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:26.336
But I'm not a victim.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:28.297
That's only because you survived.

00:01:30.841 --> 00:01:35.429
Duality of purpose, duality of motive,
is something that's constantly explored.

00:01:35.512 --> 00:01:38.640
It's all about the double meanings
and what lies beneath.

00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:45.063
You'll be constantly guessing
which person you should be rooting for.

00:01:45.147 --> 00:01:48.192
Every single episode,
cards are turned over,

00:01:48.275 --> 00:01:50.819
and the unexpected becomes the reality.

